#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:5
#: 189dc0a154a14c3da882e01e56617f8d
msgid "GPS Failsafe and Glitch Protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:7
#: 059288d9b58a413aa70f70d749099655
msgid ""
"This article describes the glitch protection mechanisms used to trigger "
"GPS Failsafe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:11
#: 4541feef15094730a526d6809ca64f80
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:13
#: aa253817480546cc88326eaf51ad5742
msgid ""
"GPS Systems can occasionally drop the signal or provide significantly "
"inaccurate position information (aka \"glitches\"). While errors are more"
" likely in conditions where the GPS signal can bounce off multiple paths "
"before reaching the receiver (multipathing), errors can occasionally "
"occur even with clear sky."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:19
#: 4f5d92091e174b86bfa2eaf41e4c5064
msgid ""
"A *GPS failsafe* event will occur if GPS 3D lock or the position "
"\"Glitches\" for at least 5 seconds while Copter is in a mode that "
"requires the GPS (RTL, Auto, Loiter, Circle, Position, Guided or Drift)."
"  The GPS failsafe response can be set to Land or switch to AltHold mode "
"so that you can retake manual control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:26
#: 73e0afe2f4c74d7f99c3673c73a2ebae
msgid ""
"Without GPS updates, the inertial sensors allow approximately 10 seconds "
"of accurate position information but after this the horizontal position "
"drift becomes so large that the horizontal position cannot be maintained "
"at all.  At this point if you still have RC radio control it is "
"recommended to take back control using Stabilize, Acro or AltHold as soon"
" as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:34
#: 9b2088006e4c436f8b19904c9aeed57b
msgid "Glitch Protection - Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:36
#: b0d0ed35765247359cbd4dd2b180e548
msgid ""
"GPS glitch protection is provided which can help alert the pilot to a bad"
" GPS position, trigger a failsafe and reduce the incidents of fly-aways."
"  Glitches are detected by comparing the each new position update "
"received from the GPS with a position projected out from the previous "
"update's position and velocity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:45
#: e3d4cabbaa9b49a898cf98f0e8ac281f
msgid "The new position is accepted as \"good\" if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:47
#: 2912de864fab44d8921c923a871ac805
msgid "the two positions are within the ``GPSGLITCH_RADIUS`` (defaults to 5m)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:49
#: 6ec05035c5b645ce9034e53efeae7517
msgid ""
"the new position is within a radius that is 10m/s/s (``GPSGLITCH_ACCEL``)"
" \\* dt \\* dt.  Where \"dt\" is the time difference between the two "
"samples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:53
#: 65091cba7bc54a3a9410393dbc45fb47
msgid ""
"During a glitch, \"Bad Position\" will be written on the ground station's"
" HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:57
#: 9644dbac37b94a588cfd67b4e3840cde
msgid "Glitch Protection - EKF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:59
#: 78b2ba8ee6ac41d1946c5017fd1600a8
msgid ""
":ref:`ArduPilot Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) <common-apm-navigation-"
"extended-kalman-filter-overview>`)provided glitch protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:62
#: 584637be305c4bddbf5ef192cb71bc47
msgid "Glitch protection using the EKF works as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:64
#: 08d65262bfad4faca155bebdf2d15f69
msgid ""
"When new GPS position measurements are received, they are compared to a "
"position predicted using IMU measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:66
#: 62f72e40cc8044be95554c9b165a635c
msgid ""
"If the difference exceeds a statistical confidence level set by "
"``EKF_POS_GATE``, then the measurement won't be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:68
#: 446b2407b32242d38a1f062bd929306e
msgid ""
"While GPS measurements aren't being used, a circle defined by an "
"uncertainty radius grows around the predicted position. The rate at which"
" this radius grows is controlled by ``EKF_GLITCH_ACCEL``. This is similar"
" to the circle defined by ``GPSGLITCH_ACCEL``, the difference being it is"
" centered around the trajectory predicted by the IMU rather than previous"
" GPS measurements. Because this allows for deviations in trajectory due "
"to maneuvers, the default value for ``EKF_GLTCH_ACCEL`` is smaller at 1.5"
" m/s/s. The acceleration growth of the circle is also increased when the "
"vehicle is accelerating or turning to allow for the increase in IMU "
"errors during maneuvers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:78
#: 5e5fcbd821ab4c05924a8e546a2035bb
msgid ""
"If subsequent GPS measurements fall inside the circle, they will be "
"accepted and the circle is reset back to the minimum radius controlled by"
" ``EKF_POS_GATE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:81
#: 049387ff91994f4ab835d48164452ad9
msgid ""
"If the GPS glitch is large enough and lasts long enough, the GPS "
"measurements will continue to be rejected until the circle radius exceeds"
" a value set by ``EKF_GLITCH_RAD``. When this happens, an offset is "
"applied to the GPS position so that it matches the estimated vehicle "
"position and the GPS positions are used again. The GPS offset is then "
"reduced to zero at 1 m/s. This means that large long duration glitches "
"will cause the vehicle to drift at a 1 m/s rate. This is slow enough to "
"give the operator plenty of time to react."
msgstr ""

